 # Octree and Tree Traversal
-Also called: Hierarchical Ray Traversal, Sparse Voxel Octree Traversal
+
+Also called: Sparse Voxel Octree (SVO) Traversal, Hierarchical Ray Traversal
 
 ## Overview
-Octree and Tree Traversal methods solve the problem of efficiently intersecting rays with sparse, hierarchical volumetric data by skipping empty space, avoiding the computational cost of sampling every voxel in a uniform grid [S6, unofficial]. Unlike standard rasterization which requires mesh generation, these methods render the entire scene with a single draw call by traversing the tree structure along ray paths [S6, unofficial]. They differ from their siblings, such as [Octree Path Computation](897-octree-path-computation.md), by explicitly managing the hierarchical descent and backtracking logic to handle irregular sparsity, rather than relying solely on precomputed paths or fixed-step rasterization [S2, S3, S6, unofficial].
+Octree and Tree Traversal methods efficiently render volumetric data by traversing a hierarchical spatial index (typically an octree) to skip empty or uniform regions, avoiding the computational cost of sampling every voxel in a uniform grid. Unlike [Digital Differential Analyzer (DDA) Traversal](3061-digital-differential-analyzer-dda-traversal.md) which steps through a fixed uniform grid, these methods adapt their step size to the tree's hierarchy, descending into occupied nodes and ascending when empty subtrees are encountered.
 
